arten entre 66 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.400 euros, se adjudicó en septiembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a circunstancias como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No hay evidencia de irregularidades en los procesos.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite abarcan necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 88 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 16.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.9 to 7.3. December accounts for 15% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 16% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 66 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,400 euros, was awarded in September 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be close to the limit due to market conditions or budget constraints. The statistical trend alone doesn't indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the contracts to see if they align with market rates. Review the awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or need. Look at the distribution of contracts across different months to identify any unusual patterns.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["I8oR84lVPkTua%2Fi14w%2FPLA%3D%3D","mXNTjdEXD41%2BF6L2uCfUWg%3D%3D","tADni%2BtbPb%2BIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"